{"parentUuid":"f726783c-4652-4486-9e90-cfae7d38e7a3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/devin/repos/a2-ai/test-build-processes","sessionId":"7f22a452-0af5-4c0c-be1c-699e971cf878","version":"2.0.22","gitBranch":"main","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"https://github.com/goreleaser/nfpm/releases/tag/v2.43.4 are the release assets to consider. You also have access to goreleaser-pro, use that and install from https://github.com/goreleaser/goreleaser-pro/releases/tag/v2.12.5 so you don't need to install go that will speed up thte build time. The GORELEASER_KEY is set as an environment variable in github actions. This may help with extend capabilities. In particular check out the pre-built binaries: https://goreleaser.com/customization/prebuilt/ which seems perfect for our rust builds, and maybe https://goreleaser.com/customization/partial/ but that may not be needed with the pre-built. Whatever you end up using provide an explaination of capabilities used in a goreleaser-pro.md file in the root of the repo for future reference. You might also use the goreleaser action for install. An example shown, though this might not give the sequential control needed       - uses: goreleaser/goreleaser-action@v6\n        with:\n          distribution: goreleaser-pro\n          version: latest\n          args: <args to use>\n        env:\n          GORELEASER_KEY: ${{ secrets.GORELEASER_KEY }}"},"uuid":"7f1ed1d1-2d56-4a1d-9677-c3a1c7bbf32d","timestamp":"2025-10-18T15:34:30.389Z","thinkingMetadata":{"level":"none","disabled":true,"triggers":[]}}
